From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: synchronous CMD_DOWNLOAD_CONFIG 0x30; reinit after 0x1b

since19 queued zeroflash_download_config from IRQ (wait=0) and reported
retval=0 without write_message(CMD_DOWNLOAD_CONFIG) completing. It also
forced need_app_config when all need_* bits were 0, then skipped
touch_reinit because touch_init already used the default report config
(no GET_TOUCH_REPORT_CONFIG 0x25).

since20:
- Follow stock need_* bits. Do not fake need_app_config. Log
  "no need_* bits, skip 0x30" and still run touch_reinit.
- 0x30 is blocking write_message from process context (wait=1). ISR
  defers (write_message is not ISR-safe). Timeout is logged; never
  ran=1 wait=0 retval=0.
- After 0x30, log status/plen/retval and GPIO/ATTN. If ATTN is high,
  drain properly (idle-bus stop stays).
- After 0x1b this boot, always identify+touch_reinit (0x25) even if
  touch_init already ok. No ENABLE_REPORT 0x05. No do_polling.
  Keep in_hdl_mode=0.

Applies after syna-tcm-hdl-status-config.patch.

